Subject: [PATCH] step0: instrumentation helpers 520-523 and launch geometry
 log (experiment only)

Throwaway build for the GPU map design study (step 0, checks 7 and 9).
Never push; not for the dev branch.

- trampoline: read-only helpers 520 (activemask as u64), 521 (%gridid),
  522 (%nsmid), 523 (%nwarpid); trampoline_ptx.h regenerated with
  clang++-16. Registered in ptxpass_core next to 509-511.
- nv_attach_impl_frida_setup.cpp: with BPFTIME_EXP_GEOMETRY_LOG naming a
  file, the cudaLaunchKernel(_ptsz), cuLaunchKernel and graph kernel-node
  add/set-params hooks (v1, v2) append one tab-separated line at entry,
  before any early return: CLOCK_MONOTONIC ns, tid, nesting depth, hook,
  kernel name (cuFuncGetName; runtime pointers via cudaGetFuncBySymbol,
  else cuKernelGetName for a CUDA 13 kernel handle; cached per pointer;
  cudart's pending error left alone), pointer, grid, block, dynamic shared
  memory, capture status, stream, graph and node handles. One O_APPEND fd,
  write(2) under a mutex. Nothing changes without the variable.

